Author: ci <ci@ferroxlabs.local>
Date:   Thu Jul 30 21:13:28 2026 +0700

    fix(cron): unblock Windows CI clippy and reap the unlaunched lease child
    
    crates/wcore-cron/tests/single_owner.rs failed `just lint`
    (cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings) on the
    ferrox-win-msvc self-hosted runner with two deny-level lints, which
    aborted the job at the Clippy step and left "Run tests (nextest CI
    profile)" SKIPPED. Every completed Windows self-hosted CI job in the
    last 40 runs failed this way, so Windows CI has been producing no test
    signal at all.
    
    - clippy::collapsible_if -> let-chain (workspace is edition 2024).
    - clippy::zombie_processes -> spawn_child returned the child on the
      success path but leaked it on the START-marker timeout path. Kill and
      wait before panicking. This is a real leak, not just a lint: the child
      may still take the lease, so an orphan would hold the exclusion the
      next case contends against and turn one failure into a cascade. On
      Windows there is no process group to collect it.
    
    Neither lint is suppressed; no test is weakened, re-gated or re-timed.
    Verified on SeanDesktop at this tree: single_owner 11 passed / 0 failed
    / 0 ignored / 0 filtered out, unchanged from before the fix.

